      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test checks `StrMatcher.StringMatcher.isMatch` with three boundary scenarios: match allowed, match within restricted range, and match blocked by a tight `bufferEnd`. I'll improve understandability by adding descriptive assertion messages, named local variables for the positional arguments, and clearer per-case comments.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version adds descriptive assertion messages, named local variables for `bufferStart`/`bufferEnd`, and per-case comments that explain the active window semantics and why each call returns 2 or 0."
